# Give the AIdrone node a stable interface name.
#
# Without this the kernel names a CDC-NCM adapter `enx<mac>` - derived from the
# device's MAC, so it differs per board and there is nothing a shipped
# NetworkManager profile could match on. Renaming to `aidrone0` is what makes
# the connection profile beside this file possible at all.
#
# The ids are the node's own, and the PID is not the ESP32-S3 default: 0x8AD1
# was chosen over the stock 0x1001 because a Zadig/libwdi INF claims
# `USB\VID_303A&PID_1001&MI_02` for WinUSB on Windows and outranks the in-box
# NCM driver. Linux does not care, but the firmware ships one PID for both
# hosts, so this is the one to match.
SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", ATTRS{idVendor}=="303a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8ad1", NAME="aidrone0"
